{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["They said: <b>How awesome</b> — each of Your deeds, like: בנות צעדה עלי שור (the daughters trod upon me like oxen)." "The sense of <b>shall lie</b> — they shall testify that falsehood and deceit are in their hand."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {0 "The quoted phrase appears to be from Judges 5:27; Ibn Ezra cites it elliptically and the construction is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:49.630723513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}